      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="682496154">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-30T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="12442378">mikefromcanmore</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP221 Wetaskiwin.  Parked just before the bridge and made the quick walk to GZ.  Cap was quickly spotted and we ran back to the truck before the rain showers moved in.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682015628">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-29T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6887855">JREnarson</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP221 - Wetaskiwin&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After the &quot;kind of found&quot; cap near Millet, this one was much easier to find and to log.  A quick pull over to the side of the road near the CP overpass just north of Wetaskiwin.  &quot;J&quot; and the geo-kids hopped out to grab this one while &quot;R&quot; watched from the geo-mobile.  Quickly found the brass cap and retrieved the required info.  Back to the geo-mobile and on our way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks again for all of your work in maintaining this virtual cache over these years.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="681839139">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-25T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
